Z||000001||mrfiero||08-24-2000||02:29 AM||||The '87 tank will not work on your '84.  In '87 GM went with a bigger tank (11.9 gal. vs 10.2 gal.).....it physically won't fit in your "tunnel".<P>I have a gas tank from an '85 coupe that will work on your '84.  It's still attached to the car, but I will be yanking the motor out this weekend and I'll take out the tank while I'm there.  <P>I believe if it is thoroughly cleaned and dried (get rid of all traces of gas) that it will be shippable.  If not, then I could possibly deliver it to you (or pretty close to you) a month from now.  I plan on attending a Fiero show up in Maine (FOCONE fall show) and can bring it with me.<P>LMK how soon you need one.    ||||reg||1
Z||000002||baldlobo||08-24-2000||10:32 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrfiero:<BR><B>The '87 tank will not work on your '84.  In '87 GM went with a bigger tank (11.9 gal. vs 10.2 gal.).....it physically won't fit in your "tunnel".<P>I have a gas tank from an '85 coupe that will work on your '84.  It's still attached to the car, but I will be yanking the motor out this weekend and I'll take out the tank while I'm there.  <P>I believe if it is thoroughly cleaned and dried (get rid of all traces of gas) that it will be shippable.  If not, then I could possibly deliver it to you (or pretty close to you) a month from now.  I plan on attending a Fiero show up in Maine (FOCONE fall show) and can bring it with me.<P>LMK how soon you need one.    </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>1984 gas tanks are 10.5, not 10.2.||||reg||1
